{"entity1": "Phase Change Materials", "entity2": "Thermal Management", "description": "The relation between Phase Change Materials (PCMs) and Thermal Management captures the application of phase change materials within various thermal management contexts. In general terms, phase change materials are used for thermal management and are applied in thermal management applications, most notably in the form of PCM-based thermal management systems. This establishes thermal management as a core application domain for these materials.\n\nSeveral specific application contexts define this relation. Phase change materials serve as a passive cooling technique for lithium-ion battery thermal management, and they are cited as one of the cooling strategies within battery thermal management more broadly. Beyond batteries, PCMs also function as a mechanism for thermal management in photovoltaic (PV) panels. Additionally, phase change materials are employed in thermal management and heat transfer for electronics cooling applications, demonstrating their versatility across energy storage, renewable energy, and electronics sectors.\n\nThe relevance of this relation is further reflected in contemporary research, as thermal management is an area covered by 2024 state-of-the-art literature on PCM melting dynamics. This indicates that ongoing scholarly work continues to examine the connection between the melting behavior of phase change materials and their effectiveness in thermal management, underscoring both the practical significance and the active scientific interest in this relationship."}
