{"entity1": "Paraffin", "entity2": "Phase Change Material", "description": "The relation (Paraffin, Phase Change Material) denotes the classification of paraffin as a type of Phase Change Material (PCM). At its core, paraffin is broadly identified as a phase change material, and in certain contexts it is specifically characterized as a liquid phase change material, reflecting its physical state during thermal energy storage and release processes.

