{"entity": "Electronic Switching In Phase-Change Materials", "type": "content", "description": ""Electronic Switching in Phase-Change Materials" (original German title: "Elektronisches Schalten in Phasenwechselmaterialien") is the doctoral thesis of Gunnar Bruns, completed at RWTH Aachen University. The research was conducted between 2007 and 2012, and the thesis comprises 116 pages, with the oral examination taking place on 31 January 2012. The Curriculum Vitae within the thesis contains a conference contribution citation on page 115.

The thesis examines electronic switching phenomena in phase-change materials, investigating key topics including switching speeds, threshold switching, and resistance drift. More broadly, it explores the electronic and thermal mechanisms underlying phase transitions in chalcogenide materials for non-volatile memory applications. The work addresses core research questions in phase-change memory (PCM) technology, particularly the physical mechanisms of threshold switching and resistance drift that govern the reliability of PCM devices.

