{"entity1": "Phase-Change Memory", "entity2": "Threshold Switching", "description": "The relation (Phase-Change Memory, Threshold Switching) captures the fundamental role that threshold switching plays in phase-change memory (PCM) technology. Threshold switching is a core mechanism studied in the operation of phase-change memory and is regarded as a fundamental physical mechanism underlying PCM devices. Within chalcogenide glasses, the materials central to PCM, threshold switching constitutes a foundational topic for the field.

