{"entity1": "External-Cavity Laser", "entity2": "Sb2S3", "description": "The relation (External-Cavity Laser, Sb2S3) describes the functional and structural association between an external-cavity laser and Sb2S3, a phase-change material that the laser incorporates as a core component of its design. Across all descriptions, this relationship is consistently characterized as a hybrid integration, meaning the external-cavity laser is constructed by hybrid-integrating the Sb2S3 phase-change material into its architecture rather than employing it as a passive or incidental element. The external-cavity laser thus utilizes and exploits Sb2S3 as an integrated, active element within its cavity.

Functionally, Sb2S3 serves as the tunable phase-change element within the external-cavity laser. Its primary role is to enable tuning of the laser's resonance wavelength, allowing the external-cavity resonance to be adjusted as needed. This tuning capability is described as reconfigurable, meaning the resonance wavelength can be deliberately altered and reset rather than being fixed at a single value. The relation therefore encompasses not merely the material's presence in the laser, but its purpose as the mechanism responsible for wavelength control.

The descriptions further emphasize several key performance characteristics that the Sb2S3 phase-change material brings to the external-cavity laser. The tuning it provides is non-volatile, meaning the selected wavelength state is retained without continuous power input. It is also described as stable, ensuring that the tuned resonance wavelength remains reliable over time, and as fast, indicating that wavelength adjustments can be made quickly. In combination, these attributes—non-volatile, fast, stable, and reconfigurable operation—define the distinctive advantage of using Sb2S3 in the external-cavity laser design.

In summary, the relation (External-Cavity Laser, Sb2S3) denotes a design paradigm in which an external-cavity laser hybrid-integrates Sb2S3 phase-change material to achieve non-volatile, fast, stable, and reconfigurable tuning of its resonance wavelength."}
