Analysis: This content is reference entry 31 in the References section of an academic paper on a hybrid-integrated external-cavity laser combining a silicon nitride waveguide sidewall Bragg grating with Sb2S3 phase-change material. The citation follows standard optical journal formatting and references a 2023 peer-reviewed article by K. Aryana, H. J. Kim, Md. R. Islam, et al., published in Optical Materials Express, volume 13, issue 11, pages 3277–3286. The cited work is a comparative material characterization study examining the optical and thermal properties of three chalcogenide phase-change materials—Ge2Sb2Te5 (GST), Sb2Se3, and Sb2S3—for reconfigurable photonic device applications. This reference is highly significant to the paper's foundational rationale: the proposed laser design exploits the high refractive-index contrast between the amorphous and crystalline states of Sb2S3, and this citation likely provides the measured material constants (refractive indices, extinction coefficients, thermal behavior, and phase-transition characteristics) that underpin the device simulations and design choices. The comparative nature of the cited study (including GST and Sb2Se3) also likely supports the authors' material selection justification, as Sb2S3 offers low optical absorption in the near-infrared/C-band region and non-volatile phase-transition behavior—key advantages over alternatives like GST for telecom-wavelength applications. Within the document structure, this entry appears in the References list following the Conclusion, Funding, Disclosures, and Data availability statements, positioned on page 12 (content list index 108), and is likely cited in the introduction or device design/material properties discussion sections of the paper."}
